    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0159" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/3491: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-01-21T12:00:00+01:00">January 21,
                        1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 21—9:32 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. The Secretariat has circulated the text of a note from the Ethiopian
                    Government under date of January 20<anchor n="71" xml:id="d102-f1"/> reiterating
                    the chief elements of the Ethiopian position. The note was apparently written on
                    the assumption that the Committee of Thirteen might attempt during the current
                    Council session to find a basis of conciliation under its mandate of December
                        19<anchor n="72" xml:id="d102-f2"/> “to examine the situation as a whole.”
                    The note expresses a willingness to assist the Committee but insists on being
                    kept informed of its discussions. Presumably as a warning against any procedure
                    similar to the Hoare-Laval plan the notice reaffirms the Ethiopian position in
                    regard to past agreements among the powers relative to Ethiopia and declares
                    that any settlement must conform to the principles laid down in the Committee’s
                    report of October 5.<anchor n="73" xml:id="d102-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
